explaining death loop simply as two  assassins stuck in a time loop manages  to both answer and ask  a lot of questions at the same time have  no fear because i got to see death loop  in action recently and i've got the  answers  here's everything you need to know about  arcane's latest  for more make sure to like this video  and subscribe okay  one of the two assassins is cult and the  other is juliana  colt is trapped on a mysterious island  and tasked with killing eight targets to  break the time loop that he's trapped in  you can play as juliana online invading  other people's games  so that you can keep the loop going if  you fear your chances against a real  opponent you can opt for juliana to be  ai controlled  colt and juliana are the cat and mouse  chase at the core of the game but  there's a lot more history to their  relationship than colt can remember  and that unfurls throughout it's  reminiscent of hades a roguelike that  would tell its story upon repeated loops  the conversations between the two never  repeat either because both colt and  juliana are aware of the time loop  unlike the other inhabitants of the  island of black reef  when you're playing as cult sometimes  juliana will radio you to comment on a  kill that you've just made  or if you've maybe run away from a fight  she'll radio you just to call you a  coward  this time loop takes place across one  in-game day but if you're worrying that  you'll be rushing against a timer to get  everything done  have no fear you can tackle everything  at your own pace  death also doesn't even mean the end of  a loop one of the powers we saw in  action gave you three redos per loop  so if you died you could return to the  encounter find and collect things from  your body and try again  if you die a third time though that loop  is finished  you also won't be starting completely  from scratch each time you start a new  loop  there's a resource in the game called  residium that helps you hang on to your  powers and weapons across  loops so not only will you restart with  an arsenal you'll also have more of  death loop's most important resource  knowledge the game takes place on a  mysterious island called black grief and  is inhabited by your eight targets and a  band of cult-like followers called  eternalists the island is split into  four districts  and each district can be visited at one  of four times during the day  and they change significantly throughout  the course of the day you might be able  to unlock a shortcut only at night or  maybe a visionary will pass through but  only at a certain time  according to game director dinga bakaba  the game starts by introducing you to  each district  then moving you to another until you've  visited all four  then you can choose which to go to and  at what time of day  once you decide to leave time moves on  when you get to the next one  if you go to a specific district at a  specific time to do a puzzle or maybe  follow a certain subquest and fail it  you can just leap right back into that  area and time period to try again  in a way death loop lets you make lots  of mini loops you don't just have to  keep doing the big one  if that makes sense by visiting these  locations over and over you not only get  the lay of the land and obtain  key items like keys and door codes but  you can build a plan  to take out your targets as efficiently  as possible like all of arcane's games  the setting  and the world tell a lot of the story  the island of black reef is an alternate  reality  loosely based on a 1960s aesthetic art  director sebastian mitos said that they  settled on that era because of the  carefree nature people had at the time  despite the anxieties of the cold war  people wanted to party forever  and so that filtered throughout the game  informing the look of the gadgets and  weapons as well as the music  the visionaries who live on the island  are a group of artists and scientists  who just want to live forever one  mission we saw was reminiscent  of dishonored's excellent lady boyle's  last party  in it you're tasked with killing lady  boyle at her own masked ball  but the problem is everyone is wearing  masks and her sisters are there too  in death loop one of the visionaries is  called alexis who you've seen in  trailers  as the one wearing a wolf mask similarly  you need to uncover his identity before  you can attempt to take him out  not every visionary encounter is going  to be like that but they will move  around and there are multiple ways you  can take them out  and boy are there ways to take them out  there are obviously  many types of guns to use because you're  an assassin interestingly though there's  no money in death loop ammo machines  distribute bullets freely because  if you're at a never-ending party utopia  why would you need  money if like me you loved the powers  from dishonored then you'll have plenty  to play with here  some may look familiar shift is similar  to blink or far reach  carnesis is similar to wind blast and  nexus works  in a very similar way to domino from  dishonored 2.  i mentioned reprise earlier which gives  you these extra redos but there's also  ether which makes you invisible  now seriously arcane where was that one  in dishonored  these powers use mana but you can use  trinkets to increase your maximum amount  trinkets are slottable items that can  also give you little perks like  dealing more damage or a cool double  jump if you play dishonored and you're  familiar with bone charms it's something  similar  when you kill an enemy whether by power  gun or simply kicking them off a ledge  their body doesn't lie around just  waiting to give you away  it kind of disintegrates so while i'm  not sure just yet if there's going to be  an incentive to do a clean hands or  ghost run like in dishonored  i wouldn't be surprised when it comes to  multiplayer it's woven into the campaign  arcane's approach to designing it is  that they want to incentivize creative  play  and hopefully the mode will be seen as  something of an anecdote generator  according to dinga  as juliana you can invade random games  or your friends and the game gives you a  list of feats to accomplish doing so  gives you points which you can then use  to unlock  new powers trinkets or weapons these  unlock randomly so you'll get different  loadouts every time you play  by playing the multiplayer component you  can unlock new appearances for cult and  juliana  so the incentivization there is  obviously the costumes you'll unlock and  the high scores but arcane genuinely  seem very excited to just see the clips  and  hear the stories of how players are  gonna be interacting online  one final thing to note about death loop  is that it is genuinely very very  funny so typically in arcane games the  humor would come from all of these  gameplay systems interacting  whereas in death loop they have made a  real effort to have the voiced  characters be really  genuinely quite funny i'm really looking  forward to it  i don't like watching you die i like  killing you  there's a difference  so to sum up defloop is some parts a  natural evolution of past arcane games  and something else altogether  it's a ps5 exclusive for a while and  we'll have more on it throughout the  year so make sure to like this video and  subscribe check out tomorrow's preview  on gamespot.com for more from dinger and  sebastian  and we'll catch you in the next loop bye  you
 

